  "verbalization": "Calabaxanthone is implicated in the regulation of Prelamin-A/C through a multi-step mechanism involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a target for Pseudopterosin Q, which in turn targets Prelamin-A/C. The evidence suggests that Calabaxanthone modulates the proteasome pathway, potentially affecting the degradation of Prelamin-A/C. The scores from the two paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with the second path providing a more detailed molecular description of the target compound. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of a key regulatory subunit in the proteasome, which could influence the stability or degradation of Prelamin-A/C. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Calabaxanthone in modulating the proteasome system, which may have implications for cellular processes involving nuclear protein degradation and structural integrity.",
